# ===========================================================
# PLACEHOLDER ONLY — NOT DEPLOYED, NOT AUTHORITATIVE
# ===========================================================
# The real ssl_bump.acl is RUNTIME STATE generated by the Web UI
# (compile_device_policies_acls in webui/app.py) and lives only on the
# NAS volume at /share/Container/squid-proxy/configs/.
#
# deploy-squid-docker.sh deliberately does NOT copy this file. It used to,
# which wiped the live per-device bump rules on every deploy and — because
# rules.acl scopes its denies to '!CONNECT' — left the proxy FAIL-OPEN:
# every blocked HTTPS site tunnelled straight through.
#
# This file is git-ignored going forward. If you still see it tracked, run:
#     git rm --cached configs/ssl_bump.acl
